Can you tell me what changes here?

00:27:20.880 --> 00:27:24.700
What's the biggest change between playing story mode

00:27:24.700 --> 00:27:27.580
and playing the nine-ball game?

00:27:28.100 --> 00:27:32.280
Well, the context is different in that when you win a game,

00:27:32.300 --> 00:27:37.000
you are treated to the moment after you win,

00:27:37.000 --> 00:27:39.720
and you immediately seduce a young lady next to you,

00:27:40.840 --> 00:27:43.520
and then she just challenges you to a trick shot,

00:27:43.620 --> 00:27:45.760
and then you move on.

00:27:45.900 --> 00:27:48.180
But if you don't do well, she's not into it.

00:27:48.240 --> 00:27:50.100
She's not into it anymore. It depends on your points.

00:27:50.240 --> 00:27:54.480
Yeah, yeah. There's certain times where she will have a bunch of hearts over her,

00:27:54.540 --> 00:27:56.280
and then there's other times where she's going to get a hand.

00:27:56.280 --> 00:27:57.120
Oh, you know what? I didn't know that.

00:27:57.220 --> 00:27:59.280
Yeah, no, it's true. You need a certain amount of points.

00:27:59.360 --> 00:28:01.740
There's a hand? Yeah, if you do bad, she does the...

00:28:01.740 --> 00:28:03.100
I think she does the hand in your face,

00:28:03.160 --> 00:28:04.080
kind of turn their back on you.

00:28:05.280 --> 00:28:07.360
So there's a couple things to set up story mode here.

00:28:07.940 --> 00:28:10.520
So just starting at the very beginning when you're at the city level,

00:28:10.520 --> 00:28:14.140
it basically says you need to get 3,100 points to move on,

00:28:14.220 --> 00:28:15.240
which is fairly easy.

00:28:15.480 --> 00:28:18.060
You don't have all the balls, though.

00:28:18.080 --> 00:28:20.540
I think you only have six in this particular instance,

00:28:20.540 --> 00:28:22.340
so it sets up just the six balls.

00:28:22.680 --> 00:28:24.520
You've got to hit them in the order,

00:28:25.000 --> 00:28:26.280
and you want to streak them.

00:28:26.580 --> 00:28:30.820
If you don't get two in a row, you start to lose lives.

00:28:30.820 --> 00:28:34.160
And once you lose, your lives are represented by balls as well.

00:28:34.320 --> 00:28:35.460
And I think you get five.

00:28:35.740 --> 00:28:38.520
And then once you lose all five, it's game over.

00:28:38.560 --> 00:28:40.960
And that's just throughout the entire story mode.

00:28:41.160 --> 00:28:49.300
So... You can regenerate balls, whether it be from hitting balls into called...

00:28:49.300 --> 00:28:52.620
I don't know what the mechanic is, but it's like...

00:28:52.620 --> 00:28:54.320
I think of it as a called shot.

00:28:55.200 --> 00:28:56.600
But you don't get to choose.

00:28:56.820 --> 00:29:01.080
You don't get to choose. It just sort of happens, and that's how they portray it.

00:29:01.120 --> 00:29:02.880
Basically, a star will appear in one pocket,

00:29:03.020 --> 00:29:05.800
and you're going to do better if you shoot in that pocket.

00:29:05.880 --> 00:29:08.720
But apparently, also, if you scratch into that pocket,

00:29:08.760 --> 00:29:11.180
you get a really weird bonus.

00:29:11.560 --> 00:29:13.900
Yes. Really? Yeah, it depends on which one it is,

00:29:13.980 --> 00:29:16.180
but I think that's the zone star one.

00:29:16.380 --> 00:29:21.280
I never attempted to just actually scratch my ball on purpose,

00:29:21.280 --> 00:29:24.780
so I never got to see this outside of watching other people play.

00:29:25.440 --> 00:29:28.020
But it was interesting to learn that, yeah.

00:29:28.280 --> 00:29:31.280
Yeah, basically, just so you can get that out of the way,

00:29:31.540 --> 00:29:35.760
if the zone star pops up and you sacrifice your cue ball in,

00:29:35.840 --> 00:29:37.040
which will cost you a life,

00:29:37.660 --> 00:29:42.560
but essentially it will change the table into a different mode

00:29:42.560 --> 00:29:46.000
where stars appear in all four corner pockets,

00:29:46.680 --> 00:29:49.460
and then the friction on the table is actually reduced.

00:29:49.460 --> 00:29:51.260
So there is a little bit of a physics thing.

00:29:51.820 --> 00:29:55.040
And then if you sink the last ball in this mode,

00:29:55.040 --> 00:29:57.180
you get multiple extra lives.

00:29:57.480 --> 00:30:00.480
Interesting. So there is like a risk-reward factor to it.

00:30:00.620 --> 00:30:02.020
